{"slug":"housing-research","label":"HOUSING RESEARCH","colour":"#FFA6A6","items":[{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","jobtitle":"Former member of the office, architect","recorded":"2014-11-05","hls":"https://customer-syg1o9n270h63juf.cloudflarestream.com/367f19c5ba47aa14514921fafa34ba07/manifest/video.m3u8","start":1311,"end":1702,"topicId":"housing-research","segments":[{"start":1311,"end":1702,"topicId":"housing-research"}],"cards":[{"time":1312.44,"title":"Housing research","id":"housing-research"},{"time":1319.68,"title":"Potteries Thinkbelt housing types","id":"potteries-thinkbelt-housing-types"},{"time":1393.16,"title":"Buckminster Fuller","id":"buckminster-fuller"},{"time":1401.32,"title":"Steel House competition","id":"steel-house-competition"},{"time":1549.2,"title":"GLC","id":"glc"},{"time":1639.24,"title":"Cedric Price Office","id":"cedric-price-office"}]}],"cards":{"Buckminster Fuller":{"slug":"buckminster-fuller","body":"Richard Buckminster \"Bucky\" Fuller published more than 30 books, coining or popularizing terms such as \"<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spaceship_Earth\">Spaceship Earth</a>\", <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ephemeralization\">ephemeralization</a>, and <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Synergetics_(Fuller)\">synergetic</a>. He also developed numerous inventions, mainly architectural designs, and popularized the widely known <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geodesic_dome\">geodesic dome</a>. Carbon molecules known as <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fullerene\">fullerenes</a> were later named by scientists for their resemblance to geodesic spheres. Buckminster Fuller was the second president of <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mensa_International\">Mensa</a> from 1974 to 1983.","subtitle":"Neo-futuristic architect, systems theorist, author, designer, and inventor.","image":"/cedric-price-memory-bank/cards/buckminster-fuller.jpg","external":"https://bfi.org","location":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/Milton,+MA,+USA/@42.2495321,-71.0661653,7z","also":[{"slug":"hans-ulrich-obrist","name":"Hans Ulrich Obrist","time":438.2,"topicId":"thinking","topicLabel":"Thinking"},{"slug":"hans-ulrich-obrist","name":"Hans Ulrich Obrist","time":1350.68,"topicId":"institutions","topicLabel":"Institutions"},{"slug":"paul-finch","name":"Paul Finch","time":123.44,"topicId":"personality","topicLabel":"Personality"},{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","time":549.32,"topicId":"potteries-thinkbelt","topicLabel":"POTTERIES THINKBELT"},{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","time":1393.16,"topicId":"housing-research","topicLabel":"HOUSING RESEARCH"}]},"Cedric Price Office":{"slug":"cedric-price-office","body":"","subtitle":null,"image":null,"external":null,"location":null,"also":[{"slug":"brett-steele","name":"Brett Steele","time":444.04,"topicId":"office","topicLabel":"Office"},{"slug":"jeremy-melvin","name":"Jeremy Melvin","time":1751.88,"topicId":"office","topicLabel":"Office"},{"slug":"john-frazer","name":"John Frazer","time":43.4,"topicId":"drawing","topicLabel":"Drawing"},{"slug":"max-neal","name":"Max Neal","time":1.64,"topicId":"office","topicLabel":"Office"},{"slug":"max-neal","name":"Max Neal","time":314.44,"topicId":"office","topicLabel":"Office"},{"slug":"max-neal","name":"Max Neal","time":442.6,"topicId":"office","topicLabel":"Office"},{"slug":"paul-barker","name":"Paul Barker","time":184.12,"topicId":"pop-up-parliament","topicLabel":"POP UP PARLIAMENT"},{"slug":"paul-barker","name":"Paul Barker","time":247.32,"topicId":"pop-up-parliament","topicLabel":"POP UP PARLIAMENT"},{"slug":"paul-barker","name":"Paul Barker","time":1065.2,"topicId":"office","topicLabel":"Office"},{"slug":"paul-finch","name":"Paul Finch","time":1063.84,"topicId":"conscience","topicLabel":"Conscience"},{"slug":"peter-murray","name":"Peter Murray","time":272.16,"topicId":"personality","topicLabel":"Personality"},{"slug":"samantha-hardingham","name":"Samantha Hardingham","time":181.32,"topicId":"office","topicLabel":"Office"},{"slug":"samantha-hardingham","name":"Samantha Hardingham","time":466.6,"topicId":"office","topicLabel":"Office"},{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","time":26.88,"topicId":"personality","topicLabel":"Personality"},{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","time":716.28,"topicId":"potteries-thinkbelt","topicLabel":"POTTERIES THINKBELT"},{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","time":743.6,"topicId":"office","topicLabel":"Office"},{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","time":1639.24,"topicId":"housing-research","topicLabel":"HOUSING RESEARCH"},{"slug":"will-alsop","name":"Will Alsop","time":2.64,"topicId":"interaction-centre","topicLabel":"INTERACTION CENTRE"},{"slug":"will-alsop","name":"Will Alsop","time":568.32,"topicId":"office","topicLabel":"Office"},{"slug":"will-alsop","name":"Will Alsop","time":672,"topicId":"office","topicLabel":"Office"},{"slug":"will-alsop","name":"Will Alsop","time":761.16,"topicId":"office","topicLabel":"Office"}]},"GLC":{"slug":"glc","body":"<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The Greater London Council (GLC) was the top-tier <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Local_government\">local government</a> administrative body for <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_London\">Greater London</a> from 1965 to 1986. It replaced the earlier <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London_County_Council\">London County Council</a> (LCC) which had covered a much smaller area. The GLC was dissolved in 1986 by the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Local_Government_Act_1985\">Local Government Act 1985</a> and its powers were devolved to the London boroughs and other entities.</p>","subtitle":"Greater London Council","image":"/cedric-price-memory-bank/cards/glc.jpg","external":"http://news.bbc.co.uk/onthisday/hi/dates/stories/march/31/newsid_2530000/2530803.stm","location":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/London,+UK/@51.5073509,-0.1277583,7z","also":[{"slug":"max-neal","name":"Max Neal","time":205.2,"topicId":"building","topicLabel":"Building"},{"slug":"max-neal","name":"Max Neal","time":492.2,"topicId":"southbank","topicLabel":"SOUTHBANK"},{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","time":143,"topicId":"potteries-thinkbelt","topicLabel":"POTTERIES THINKBELT"},{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","time":1549.2,"topicId":"housing-research","topicLabel":"HOUSING RESEARCH"}]},"Housing research":{"slug":"housing-research","body":"Research into flexible, pre-fabricated, short life housing in the UK. Published in AD in 1971.","subtitle":"Cedric Price architects","image":"/cedric-price-memory-bank/cards/housing-research.png","external":"http://www.aaschool.ac.uk/PUBLIC/AAPUBLICATIONS/aboutpublications.php","location":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/United+Kingdom/@55.378051,-3.435973,7z","also":[{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","time":1312.44,"topicId":"housing-research","topicLabel":"HOUSING RESEARCH"}]},"Potteries Thinkbelt housing types":{"slug":"potteries-thinkbelt-housing-types","body":"Four types of housing were designed: crate, battery, capsule and sprawl. All are designed by name to goad a profession hard-wired into rejecting such terms having any relation to the sacrosanct Vitruvian principles of ‘commodity, firmness and delight’.","subtitle":"Crate, battery, capsule and sprawl","image":"/cedric-price-memory-bank/cards/potteries-thinkbelt-housing-types.jpg","external":"http://www.amazon.com/Cedric-Price-Potteries-Thinkbelt-SuperCrit/dp/0415434122","location":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/Madeley,+Staffordshire,+UK/@52.997861,-2.339182,7z","also":[{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","time":232.04,"topicId":"potteries-thinkbelt","topicLabel":"POTTERIES THINKBELT"},{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","time":612.24,"topicId":"potteries-thinkbelt","topicLabel":"POTTERIES THINKBELT"},{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","time":1319.68,"topicId":"housing-research","topicLabel":"HOUSING RESEARCH"}]},"Steel House competition":{"slug":"steel-house-competition","body":"Cedric Price designed the Steelhouse as a response to the increasing requirements for less definitive space. He argued that the main design criterion should be for the provision of space with maximum variation of possible uses. Features of the plan are: a shared activity area that is variable over a 24-hour cycle; alternative access routes (internal and external); capacity for subdivision into 2 homes; possibility of permanently fragmented ‘home’ with self-contained units and separate external access.","subtitle":"Cedric Price architects","image":"/cedric-price-memory-bank/cards/steel-house-competition.jpg","external":"http://www.aaschool.ac.uk/PUBLIC/AAPUBLICATIONS/aboutpublications.php","location":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/United+Kingdom/@55.378051,-3.435973,7z","also":[{"slug":"steve-mullin","name":"Steve Mullin","time":1401.32,"topicId":"housing-research","topicLabel":"HOUSING RESEARCH"}]}}}